decks.find(deck => deck.id === "akiza").combos.push({"title":"Roxrose and White Rose into Black Rose Dragon","hand":"Roxrose Dragon + White Rose Dragon","condition":"Your field is empty, and Basal Rose Shoot and Black Rose Dragon remain in your Deck and Extra Deck.","steps":["Normal Summon Roxrose Dragon and use its effect to add Basal Rose Shoot from your Deck to your hand.","Special Summon White Rose Dragon from your hand while you control Roxrose Dragon, a Dragon Tuner.","Synchro Summon Black Rose Dragon using Level 3 Roxrose and Level 4 White Rose. You may decline Black Rose Dragon’s optional destruction effect.","Activate Basal Rose Shoot to Special Summon Roxrose Dragon from your Graveyard in Defense Position. Its search effect was already used this turn."],"result":"Black Rose Dragon and Roxrose Dragon, with White Rose Dragon and Basal Rose Shoot in the Graveyard."});
decks.find(deck => deck.id === "crow").combos.push({"title":"Boreastorm into Blackwing Full Armor Master","hand":"Blackwing - Sudri the Phantom Glimmer + Blackwing - Vata the Emblem of Wandering","condition":"Your field is empty; Shamal and Black Feather Whirlwind are in the Deck. Boreastorm and Full Armor Master are in the Extra Deck.","steps":["Normal Summon Sudri. Its effect adds Shamal from the Deck to your hand.","Send Shamal from your hand to the Graveyard to place Black Feather Whirlwind face-up in a Spell & Trap Zone.","Special Summon Vata from your hand because you control another Blackwing monster.","Synchro Summon Boreastorm using Level 4 Sudri and Level 2 Vata.","Activate Black Feather Whirlwind to Special Summon Sudri from the Graveyard. Boreastorm is already Level 6, so its optional effect is unnecessary. Decline Shamal’s optional Graveyard effect.","Synchro Summon Blackwing Full Armor Master using Level 6 Boreastorm as the Blackwing Tuner and Level 4 Sudri as the non-Tuner."],"result":"Blackwing Full Armor Master and Black Feather Whirlwind remain on the field."});
decks.find(deck => deck.id === "yusei").combos.push({"title":"Full-Speed Warrior into Junk Warrior Extreme","hand":"Full-Speed Warrior + any other card to discard","condition":"Start with five cards, including Full-Speed Warrior and another card to discard. If Anchorbolt Hedgehog is in your hand, it is a strong discard choice. All named searches and Synchro Monsters must remain available. Your opponent must control a monster Extreme can destroy by battle for the final step.","steps":["Normal Summon Full-Speed Warrior and add Synchro Fellowship from your Deck to your hand.","Activate Synchro Fellowship, add Junk Synchron and Scrap Synchron from the Deck to your hand, and discard one other card. Anchorbolt Hedgehog is a useful discard if you have it.","Synchro Summon Scrap Warrior using Full-Speed Warrior on the field and Scrap Synchron in your hand. Scrap Warrior adds Crossroad Sonic Chick from the Deck to your hand.","Banish Synchro Fellowship from your Graveyard to reduce Scrap Warrior to Level 2 and gain an additional Normal Summon. Normal Summon Junk Synchron, then use its effect to Special Summon Full-Speed Warrior from your Graveyard in Defense Position with its effects negated.","Synchro Summon Junk Speeder using Junk Synchron and Full-Speed Warrior. Activate Junk Speeder as Chain Link 1 and Crossroad Sonic Chick in your hand as Chain Link 2. Resolve Crossroad, then Special Summon Jet Synchron, Satellite Synchron, and the second Junk Synchron from the Deck with Speeder.","Synchro Summon Formula Synchron using Jet Synchron and Crossroad Sonic Chick. Banish Crossroad when it leaves the field, then use Formula Synchron’s optional effect to draw one card.","Synchro Summon Junk Warrior Extreme using Junk Synchron and Junk Speeder. Activate Extreme’s effect and Special Summon Full-Speed Warrior and Scrap Synchron from your Graveyard into your two empty Main Monster Zones. Their effects cannot be activated this turn, and only one more Special Summon is allowed this turn. If you discarded Anchorbolt Hedgehog, you can summon it instead of Scrap Synchron. The Anchorbolt branch shows how to summon it earlier while keeping Scrap Synchron.","When you can conduct your Battle Phase, have Junk Warrior Extreme destroy an opponent’s monster by battle. Banish Extreme to Special Summon Junk Warrior from the Extra Deck, treated as a Synchro Summon. Resolve Junk Warrior’s ATK gain using the Level 2 or lower monsters you control, then attack if you can. With no other modifiers, Junk Warrior reaches 10,100 ATK during this Battle Phase: 2,300 base + 6,900 from Level 2 or lower monsters + 900 from Full-Speed Warrior. The 6,900 includes Full-Speed’s boosts to itself, Scrap Warrior, and Scrap Synchron."],"result":"Scrap Warrior at Level 2, Formula Synchron, Satellite Synchron, Full-Speed Warrior and Scrap Synchron, plus Junk Warrior Extreme. Extreme can become Junk Warrior after destroying a monster by battle. Junk Warrior reaches 10,100 ATK during the illustrated Battle Phase with no other modifiers."});
decks.find(deck => deck.id === "yusei").combos.push({"title":"Full-Speed Warrior into Stardust Warrior","hand":"Full-Speed Warrior + any other card to discard","condition":"Start with Full-Speed Warrior and another card to discard. All named searches and Synchro Monsters must be available. The illustrated follow-up requires the opponent to destroy Stardust Warrior by card effect.","steps":["Normal Summon Full-Speed Warrior and add Synchro Fellowship from your Deck to your hand.","Activate Synchro Fellowship, add Junk Synchron and Scrap Synchron from the Deck to your hand, and discard one other card. Anchorbolt Hedgehog is a useful discard if you have it.","Synchro Summon Scrap Warrior using Full-Speed Warrior on the field and Scrap Synchron in your hand. Scrap Warrior adds Crossroad Sonic Chick from the Deck to your hand.","Banish Synchro Fellowship from your Graveyard to reduce Scrap Warrior to Level 2 and gain an additional Normal Summon. Normal Summon Junk Synchron, then use its effect to Special Summon Full-Speed Warrior from your Graveyard in Defense Position with its effects negated.","Synchro Summon Junk Speeder using Junk Synchron and Full-Speed Warrior. Activate Junk Speeder as Chain Link 1 and Crossroad Sonic Chick in your hand as Chain Link 2. Resolve Crossroad, then Special Summon Jet Synchron, Satellite Synchron, and the second Junk Synchron from the Deck with Speeder.","Synchro Summon Formula Synchron using Jet Synchron and Crossroad Sonic Chick. Banish Crossroad when it leaves the field, then use Formula Synchron’s optional effect to draw one card.","Synchro Summon Accel Synchro Stardust Dragon using Level 5 Junk Speeder and Level 3 Junk Synchron. Activate Accel’s effect to Special Summon Scrap Synchron from your Graveyard.","Synchro Summon Stardust Warrior using Level 8 Accel Synchro Stardust Dragon and Level 2 Formula Synchron. Keep Scrap Warrior, Scrap Synchron, and Satellite Synchron on the field.","If your opponent destroys Stardust Warrior by a card effect, activate its effect to Special Summon Junk Warrior Extreme from the Extra Deck, treated as a Synchro Summon. Activate Extreme to Special Summon Full-Speed Warrior and Jet Synchron from the Graveyard into the two open Main Monster Zones. Their effects cannot be activated this turn, and you can Special Summon only one more time that turn."],"result":"Stardust Warrior threatens to negate an opponent’s Special Summon. If it is destroyed by battle or leaves the field because of an opponent’s card effect, it can bring out Junk Warrior Extreme. The illustrated follow-up shows destruction by card effect; tributing Stardust Warrior for its own negation does not trigger its leaving-field effect."});
decks.find(deck => deck.id === "yusei").combos.push({"title":"Full-Speed Warrior with Anchorbolt discard","hand":"Full-Speed Warrior + Anchorbolt Hedgehog","condition":"Start with Full-Speed Warrior, Anchorbolt Hedgehog and three other cards. All searched cards and Synchro Monsters remain available. The final step requires an opposing monster Extreme can destroy by battle.","steps":["Normal Summon Full-Speed Warrior and add Synchro Fellowship from your Deck to your hand.","Activate Synchro Fellowship, add Junk Synchron and Scrap Synchron from your Deck to your hand, and discard Anchorbolt Hedgehog.","Synchro Summon Scrap Warrior using Full-Speed Warrior on the field and Scrap Synchron in your hand. Scrap Warrior adds Crossroad Sonic Chick from the Deck to your hand.","Banish Synchro Fellowship to reduce Scrap Warrior to Level 2 and gain an additional Normal Summon. Normal Summon Junk Synchron and use its effect to Special Summon Full-Speed Warrior from your Graveyard with its effects negated.","Activate Anchorbolt Hedgehog in your Graveyard while you control Scrap Warrior, which mentions Junk Warrior. Special Summon Anchorbolt in Defense Position.","Synchro Summon Junk Speeder with Junk Synchron and Full-Speed Warrior. Activate Speeder as Chain Link 1 and Crossroad Sonic Chick in your hand as Chain Link 2. Resolve Crossroad, then Speeder summons Jet Synchron and the second Junk Synchron. Anchorbolt occupies the other Main Monster Zone, so there are only two open zones for Speeder.","Synchro Summon Formula Synchron using Jet Synchron and Crossroad Sonic Chick. Banish Crossroad when it leaves the field, then draw one card with Formula Synchron.","Synchro Summon Junk Warrior Extreme using Junk Synchron and Junk Speeder. Use Extreme’s effect to Special Summon Full-Speed Warrior and Scrap Synchron from the Graveyard into the two open Main Monster Zones. Their effects cannot be activated this turn, and you can Special Summon only one more time this turn.","When you can conduct your Battle Phase, have Junk Warrior Extreme destroy an opponent’s monster by battle. Banish Extreme to Special Summon Junk Warrior from the Extra Deck, treated as a Synchro Summon. Resolve Junk Warrior’s ATK gain using the Level 2 or lower monsters you control, then attack if you can. With no other modifiers, Junk Warrior reaches 11,100 ATK during this Battle Phase: 2,300 base + 7,900 from Level 2 or lower monsters + 900 from Full-Speed Warrior. The 7,900 includes Full-Speed’s boosts to itself, Anchorbolt, Scrap Warrior, and Scrap Synchron."],"result":"Scrap Warrior at Level 2, Formula Synchron, Anchorbolt Hedgehog, Full-Speed Warrior and Scrap Synchron, plus Junk Warrior Extreme. Extreme can become Junk Warrior after destroying a monster by battle. Junk Warrior reaches 11,100 ATK during the illustrated Battle Phase with no other modifiers."});
